# Agent & LLM Instructions — Vesta Engineering Conventions

> **Canonical Reference for Vesta (`com.vesta.desktop`)** — a modular Rust Cargo workspace (`core/*`, `lib/*`, `cli/*`, `apps/vesta-gui`, `apps/whisper-bench`) built with **Tauri v2 + Svelte 5 (Runes) + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS v4**.
> Read alongside [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md), [`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md), and [`docs/QUALITY.md`](docs/QUALITY.md).

---

## 0. Golden Rules

1. **Never hardcode colors.** Use semantic CSS tokens in `apps/vesta-gui/src/app.css` (`--bg`, `--surface`, `--surface-2`, `--surface-3`, `--text`, `--muted`, `--border`, `--accent`, `--accent-strong`, `--accent-text`, `--done`, `--danger`, `--control-*`, `--glass-*`).
2. **No raw browser defaults.** Never use native `<select>`, unstyled `<input type="checkbox">`, raw scrollbars where custom ones apply, or unguarded native file dialogs. Use `SearchableSelect.svelte`, `ConfirmDialog.svelte`, `AppContextMenu.svelte`, `AppTooltip.svelte`, and `dialogGuard.ts` (`guardedOpen` / `guardedSave`).
3. **One source of truth per concern.**
   - Version → [`build-scripts/PKGBUILD`](build-scripts/PKGBUILD) `pkgver` (propagated by `build-scripts/update_project_info.sh`).
   - Heavy domain logic → pure Rust crates in `core/*` and `lib/*` (never duplicated in Tauri handlers or Svelte).
   - Persisted UI state → [`apps/vesta-gui/src/lib/config/vestaConfig.ts`](apps/vesta-gui/src/lib/config/vestaConfig.ts) (never raw `localStorage`).
   - Translations → `apps/vesta-gui/src/lib/i18n/locales/en.json` + lazy-loaded per-language JSON catalogs (15 locales).
   - Code/doc contracts → [`docs/contracts_manifest.json`](docs/contracts_manifest.json) checked by `build-scripts/check_doc_contracts.py`.
   - Feature & audit tracking → `scorecard/*.toml` + [`scorecard/scorecard.db`](scorecard/scorecard.db) managed via `build-scripts/scorecard_db.py`.
4. **Keep engines decoupled from Tauri and GUI.** `core/*` and `lib/*` must remain headless, callback/cancellation-driven, and directly consumable by `cli/*`, `vesta-mcp`, and `apps/vesta-gui/src-tauri`.
5. **English code & commits.** Write all commit messages, Rust errors, logs, and code comments in **English** using Conventional Commits (§12).
6. **Accessibility & RTL.** Keyboard handlers on all custom controls, visible focus states, logical CSS properties (`ps-*`, `pe-*`, `ms-*`, `me-*`, `border-e`, `inset-inline-*`), and `dir="rtl"` support for Arabic (`ar`).

---

## 1. Tech Stack & Svelte 5 Conventions

- **Workspace**: Rust edition `2024`, `rust-version = "1.99"`, resolver `"3"`. `.cargo/config.toml` sets `WHISPER_DONT_GENERATE_BINDINGS = "1"` and uses `clang` + `mold` on `x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu`.
- **Desktop shell**: **Tauri v2** (`tauri 2.12`, GPL-3.0-only) in `apps/vesta-gui/src-tauri`.
- **Frontend**: **Svelte 5** (`^5.55`) + **TypeScript** (`^6.0`) + **Vite 8** (`port: 5175`, `strictPort: true`; keep `svelteVirtualCssFallback()` intact in `vite.config.ts`) + **Tailwind CSS v4**.
- **Runes only**: Use `$state`, `$derived`, `$props()`, `$effect`, and `{#snippet}` consistently across `.svelte` and `*.svelte.ts` modules. Do not mix legacy Svelte 4 `export let` / `$:` syntax with runes.
- **Thin components**: Extract workflow sequencing into `apps/vesta-gui/src/lib/workflows/*.ts` with injected IPC callbacks and `*.test.ts` unit tests. Route all Tauri calls through `$lib/services/tauriClient.ts` (`invokeCommand`).
- **Static AST guard (`npm run check:patterns`)**: `apps/vesta-gui/scripts/check-code-patterns.mjs` rejects `debugger`, `new Promise(async ...)`, and `array.forEach(async ...)`.

---

## 2. Design Tokens & Scroll Performance (`apps/vesta-gui/src/app.css`)

- Shared semantic classes: `.glass-card`, `.btn-primary`, `.btn-secondary`, `.btn-icon` (`2rem×2rem`), `.btn-compact`, `.btn-success`, `.btn-danger`, `.input-modern`, `.vesta-context-menu`, `.searchable-select-*`, `.progress-modern*`.
- Dropdowns use opaque `--control-menu-bg` (`#18212e`) so lists never bleed into underlying content.
- Inside `.settings-scroll`, `.glass-card` disables `backdrop-filter` and applies `contain: layout paint style` + `content-visibility: auto` to prevent continuous compositor repaints while scrolling. Preserve this rule.

---

## 3. Repository Layout

```text
vesta/
├─ Cargo.toml                     # Workspace: core/*, lib/*, cli/*, apps/*/src-tauri
├─ core/                          # Foundational zero-UI crates (vesta-parser, vesta-apkg, vesta-download)
├─ lib/                           # Headless engines (flashcards, translate, transcribe, autosync, extract, ocr, refine, sync, ankiconnect)
├─ cli/                           # vesta-cli (unified), vesta-mcp (stdio MCP, 24 tools), 8 vesta-*-cli crates
├─ apps/
│  ├─ vesta-gui/                  # Tauri v2 + Svelte 5 desktop app (`vesta`)
│  │  ├─ scripts/                 # i18n audit/scanner, AST code-pattern & UI contract checks, dev-CSS check
│  │  ├─ src/                     # main.ts, App.svelte, app.css, lib/{components,config,i18n,modals,panels,services,stores,tabs,types,utils,workflows}
│  │  └─ src-tauri/               # Tauri commands, plugin stdio host, loopback media server, updater
│  └─ whisper-bench/              # Whisper.cpp & VAD hardware benchmark utility
├─ vendor/whisper-rs-sys-0.15.0/  # Patched FFI crate pinned via [patch.crates-io]
├─ scorecard/                     # features/reliability/performance/bugs/impact_map TOMLs + tracked scorecard.db
├─ build-scripts/                 # quality_check.py, check_doc_contracts.py, scorecard_db.py, check-i18n.sh, PKGBUILD, git hooks
└─ docs/                          # Reference manuals, contracts_manifest.json, SCORECARD.md, modules/*.md
```

---

## 4. Startup Invariant, 6-Zone Shell & Tab Lifecycle

- **Startup hydration (`src/main.ts`)**: Singleton stores read `vestaConfig.getItem(...)` at module evaluation time. `main.ts` MUST `await hydrateVestaConfig()` **before** dynamically importing `$lib/i18n` (`await initI18n()`) and `./App.svelte`. Never convert those into static top-level imports.
- **Outer shell (`App.svelte` & `Sidebar.svelte`)**:
  - Fixed viewport `flex h-screen min-w-[460px] min-h-[520px]` — the outer window never scrolls.
  - Collapsible sidebar (`w-[18rem]` ↔ `w-20`) with responsive hysteresis (`1300px` collapse / `1490px` expand unless overridden by user preference); opening **Settings** swaps the sidebar nav in-place to Settings sections with a back header to `lastActiveMainTab`.
  - Bottom-left attribution dock (`h-[92px]`): author avatar, version/inbox button (`NotificationInbox.svelte`), license, sponsor modal (`SupportModal.svelte`), and GitHub link (7 clicks on the brand logo within 4s unlocks `experimental`).
- **Persistent lazy tabs**: `flashcards` and `extract` load eagerly; `refine`, `translate`, `sync`, `align`, `transcribe`, `experimental`, `settings`, and `plugins` (`plugin:<id>`) load via `createTabLoader` + idle/hover preloading and remain mounted (`class:hidden={activeTab !== ...}`) so running jobs survive tab switches.
- **Tab layout & footer (`FooterActions.svelte`)**: Full-height tabs use `.tab-layout flex flex-col h-full` with one `min-h-0 flex-1 overflow-y-auto` scroll body and `FooterActions.svelte` (`h-[92px]`, matching the sidebar footer border). Always set `min-w-0` / `min-h-0` on flex/grid wrappers around scroll containers.

---

## 5. Persistence, Easy/Expert Mode, Shortcuts, Snackbars & Dialogs

- **Config (`$lib/config/vestaConfig.ts`)**: Synchronous in-memory reads backed by serialized atomic writes to `vesta_config.json`. Call `await vestaConfig.flush()` before reloads or onboarding completion.
- **Easy vs Expert Mode (`uiModeStore.svelte.ts`)**: Disabling Expert mode backs up advanced overrides and restores safe Easy defaults (`.apkg`, `n-1` CPU workers, minimal controls).
- **Shortcuts (`utils/shortcuts.ts` + `ShortcutsTab.svelte`)**: Ignore global shortcuts when focus is inside `INPUT`, `TEXTAREA`, or `contentEditable` (`isInputActive`). Register every user-facing shortcut in `defaultShortcuts` with localized descriptions and scope-aware conflict checks.
- **Snackbars (`snackbarStore.svelte.ts`)**: Minimum durations enforced by severity (`1700ms` default, `3500ms` warning, `5000ms` error), duplicate coalescing, bounded queue (`8`), hover/focus pause.
- **Native Dialog Guard (`utils/dialogGuard.ts`)**: Always call `guardedOpen` / `guardedSave` instead of `@tauri-apps/plugin-dialog` directly; handle `null` when another dialog is in flight.

---

## 6. Localization (15 Locales, Lazy Chunks)

- **Locales**: `ar` (RTL), `de`, `en`, `es`, `fr`, `hi`, `it`, `ja`, `ko`, `nl`, `pl`, `pt`, `ru`, `tr`, `zh` in `apps/vesta-gui/src/lib/i18n/locales/*.json`.
- **Bundle split**: Only `en.json` is statically bundled; other locales load on demand via `import.meta.glob('./locales/*.json')` merged over `en`.
- **Usage**: `let t = $derived($locale);` with `{{param}}` (or `{param}`) interpolation. Update all 15 locale files in the same task and verify with `bash build-scripts/check-i18n.sh`.

---

## 7. Whisper, OCR, MCP & Declarative Plugins

- **Whisper (`lib/vesta-transcribe` + `vendor/whisper-rs-sys-0.15.0`)**: Pinned via `[patch.crates-io]` to link split GGML static archives (`whisper`, `ggml`, `ggml-base`, `ggml-cpu`), guarded by `bindgen-drift-check.yml`. Optional GPU features (`vulkan`, `cuda`, `rocm`, `sycl`) are mutually exclusive build targets (Linux desktop enables `vulkan`) and always fall back cleanly to CPU at runtime.
- **Offline & Vision OCR (`lib/vesta-ocr`)**: Pure-Rust PaddleOCR v4 ONNX (`LocalOcrBackend`, unaffected by AI Kill Switch) + Vision LLM failover (`CompositeOcrBackend`) for bitmap tracks (PGS/VobSub/DVB/XSUB) and burned-in video ROIs.
- **MCP Server (`cli/vesta-mcp`)**: `rmcp` over stdio exposing 24 tools (documented in [`docs/MCP.md`](docs/MCP.md)) with canonicalized `--read-root` / `--output-root` isolation and server-side provider profiles. Also embedded in `vesta-cli mcp` / `vesta mcp`.
- **Plugin SDK (`docs/PLUGINS.md`)**: Out-of-process JSON-RPC 2.0 stdio plugins rendered through Vesta's 26-widget schema (`PluginRenderer.svelte`) and validated with `docs/examples/plugin-hello/vesta_plugin.py`.

---

## 8. Versioning, CI/CD & Verification Gates

- **Versioning**: `build-scripts/PKGBUILD` (`pkgver`) is the sole source of truth; never bump versions or tags manually. `release.yml` runs `semantic-release` automatically on push to `main` (stable `vX.Y.Z`) and `dev` (prerelease `vX.Y.Z-dev.N`) after exact-SHA `ci.yml` succeeds, propagating versions via `update_project_info.sh`, dispatching `build.yml`, and backmerging `main` → `dev`.
- **Commits**: English Conventional Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `perf:`, `refactor:`, `docs:`, `test:`, `chore:`, `ci:`, `build:`), clear release-note subjects, 0–3 line bodies.
- **Definition of Done**:
  1. **Frontend** (`apps/vesta-gui`): `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run test:dev-css`, and `bash ../../build-scripts/check-i18n.sh` when UI copy changes.
  2. **Rust & Contracts** (repo root): `cargo fmt --all --check`, `cargo clippy --locked --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `python3 build-scripts/check_doc_contracts.py`, `python3 build-scripts/browser_ipc_contract.py --check`, `python3 build-scripts/check_library_integration.py`.
  3. **Scorecard & Gate**: Keep `docs/SCORECARD.md` (`generate_scorecard.py`) and `scorecard/scorecard.db` (`scorecard_db.py sync`) current; run `python3 build-scripts/quality_check.py` (or `--desktop --smoke` before release).
